{"step_index":308,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T00:53:05Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-15T09:53:05+09:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-15T09:53:08+09:00\nThe search for \"\"210.104.16.\"\" returned the following summary:\n\"210.104.16.\" is a prefix for a range of public IPv4 addresses[1][2]. Specifically, it refers to the block of addresses from **210.104.16.0 to 210.104.16.254**[1][2].\n\n### Key Information:\n*   **Type:** This is a public IP address range[3], which means it is routable over the internet, unlike private IP addresses (such as 10.x.x.x, 172.16.x.x, or 192.168.x.x)[3][4].\n*   **Context:** IP addresses starting with `210.104.` are generally allocated to organizations in the Asia-Pacific region[5][6].\n*   **Usage:** If you are seeing this IP address in your network logs or security reports, it indicates traffic originating from or directed to a device within that specific subnet[3].\n\nIf you are trying to identify a specific device, please note that an IP address alone typically only identifies the network or the service provider associated with that range[7][4]. Further information (such as specific port activity or logs) would be needed to determine what the device is doing[4].\n\nSources:\n[1] [ipshu.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGBYAj5tFEY4Di08HMQIKTKfZ1c-t4EkwA6Tyed9kE8n9JKB2yjyGj_Rx8O0jYP4QAwRW990g05_Z1wM8LcMh2eHzLKfREfuCNs-i9b67WpJy3IDcJVnglx5_Cb7Q==)\n[2] [ipshu.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEiyn0gXubmh9s_yFsg_jguRoQ4-hb0juudyrepGVYRglnywmaEWq1dmfUEjTOYFYRBz03m69Kv4XcrMpgfqAnJPxGqm-_JmWix4f3V4L6XknjV594nkNHNqohJxw==)\n[3] [wmtips.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEAADce-WOJLy4sU2qkqrggmFsDNqfxMefj10z1QMANPvO4u9epjMW9fjUAXLktqsG6weY6b00QAdfuzdDasuFK44I4tHmOWG7GDHBez62ldsUSVMr6AI2l1_gemQKu1b_pxKs=)\n[4] [149.210.214](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redire